SDK audio: output-stage playback rate for fable2 turbo (docs/turbo.md, "Turbo audio").
rex::audio::SetPlaybackRate(rate, mode) makes the SDL device callback consume guest frames
rate x faster than real time and squeeze them into real time with an Apple audio unit rendered
offline in the callback (AUNewTimePitch: same pitch; AUVarispeed: resampled, higher pitch).
The guest's frame credit (client semaphore) grows to base x rate x audio_rate_headroom (2), so
short guest stalls are absorbed; on the way back the extra credit becomes debt and the turbo backlog is dropped under
a one-chunk fade. Rate 1 / kNormal leaves the original direct path. Also: audio_rate_stats
(queue depth / consumption log) and audio_capture (WAV of the device output) cvars. A small
trim of the unit rate keeps input pulled equal to rate x output (up to +8%; AUNewTimePitch
pulls less than rate x output on real content) and slows the pull
(up to -20%) instead of starving when the guest audio worker falls behind.
Defines REX_AUDIO_PLAYBACK_RATE in rex/audio/downmix.h.

